# Run C report

Generated exactly once per frame with the built-in image generation tool. All three calls completed without refusals; no retries were made.

Each call edited `../ref/idle-template.png`, with `00-idle.png` and `../ref/borin-still.png` as identity references, in that order. Each used `transparent_background: true` and the absolute local reference paths. No other generated frame was used as an input.

All outputs were copied unchanged from the returned generated files. SHA-256 hashes of each saved file match its source. No resizing, compositing, background removal, alpha repair, or pixel processing was performed.

## Output verification and limitations

The tool returned **1254 Ã— 1254** for every frame, despite the exact prompts requesting 1536 Ã— 1536. PNG headers report 8-bit RGBA (colour type 6). The square shape and native alpha are retained, but these outputs do not meet the requested 1536-based pixel scale and ground coordinates. Visual inspection shows the requested sequence of kneeling, collapsing and side-lying poses. Exact anatomy, ground placement, and pose-height limits are not certified; in particular the final lying pose appears taller than the requested half-standing-height limit. Per the one-generation and unchanged-output requirements, no regeneration or correction was performed.

